00:27:26.610 --> 00:27:30.480
We look for sentences with two
quantities or conversions, so we can

00:27:30.480 --> 00:27:31.830
write down all these little givens.

00:27:32.700 --> 00:27:35.760
You'll then have to map out how
to go from one unit to the other.

00:27:35.760 --> 00:27:37.470
This might require prefixes.

00:27:37.770 --> 00:27:41.190
Those are a big hint if
you see similar units.

00:27:41.745 --> 00:27:43.785
Same thing going from us to metric.

00:27:43.875 --> 00:27:47.355
We might see the same thing to pay
attention to your measurements.

00:27:47.355 --> 00:27:48.465
Are they all masses?

00:27:48.765 --> 00:27:49.965
Are they all volumes?

00:27:50.385 --> 00:27:51.165
Are they length?

00:27:51.375 --> 00:27:52.275
Are they the same?

00:27:52.725 --> 00:27:53.415
They will help you.

00:27:54.225 --> 00:27:58.635
If you need to read the problem
slowly to find what you need, don't

00:27:58.635 --> 00:28:01.035
feel like if you read it once,
you're like, oh, I didn't find it.

00:28:01.425 --> 00:28:02.805
Go word by word.

00:28:03.015 --> 00:28:06.045
When I say problems, I say
them out loud all the time.

00:28:06.375 --> 00:28:09.315
If you're sitting at your desk, you
can say it to yourself just quietly.

00:28:09.615 --> 00:28:12.825
If that helps you do it, don't
worry about the people next to you.

00:28:12.825 --> 00:28:15.045
Unless your teacher starts
yelling at you, that's different.

00:28:15.435 --> 00:28:18.555
But if you need to kind of
word it to yourself, do it.

00:28:18.585 --> 00:28:19.485
Help yourself.

00:28:20.129 --> 00:28:24.389
Uh, let those units guide you
in your thinking because those

00:28:24.389 --> 00:28:27.450
comment units, they'll, they'll,
they'll all have to cancel, right?

00:28:27.750 --> 00:28:28.830
Opposites cancel.

00:28:29.520 --> 00:28:30.300
Look for those.

00:28:30.389 --> 00:28:32.760
Now, the last tip is don't
start with a conversion.

00:28:32.790 --> 00:28:34.170
That's not all the time.

00:28:34.590 --> 00:28:36.060
There are exceptions to that.

00:28:36.480 --> 00:28:39.420
If you were given a problem
with only conversion factors,

00:28:39.899 --> 00:28:41.460
then okay, you have no choice.

00:28:42.060 --> 00:28:45.344
If that's the case, The hint I
can give you is make sure the

00:28:45.344 --> 00:28:48.645
unit that you desire is on top.

00:28:48.645 --> 00:28:48.945
Okay?

00:28:48.945 --> 00:28:52.695
So you want it on top, so that way
on the final part of the problem,

00:28:52.695 --> 00:28:55.574
it's still up there so you can
just cancel the other units out.

00:28:56.054 --> 00:29:00.375
So start with whatever you want, where
it needs to be in the final answer.

